---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Learning path"
  description="The planned Grove curriculum for tree-based machine learning."
>
  <header class="page-header">
    <p class="eyebrow">Project roadmap</p>
    <h1>Learn from one split to a forest.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Each chapter adds one reusable idea. The sequence will grow with the code,
      so later lessons can reveal how ensembles are composed from simple trees.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="roadmap-grid">
    <article>
      <h2>1 · Foundations</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>How trees learn</li>
        <li>Gini and entropy</li>
        <li>Regression trees</li>
        <li>Depth, leaves, and overfitting</li>
      </ul>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h2>2 · Ensembles</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Bagging and bootstrap samples</li>
        <li>Random forests</li>
        <li>Gradient boosting</li>
        <li>Modern boosting systems</li>
      </ul>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h2>3 · Applications</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Failure investigations</li>
        <li>Interpretability</li>
        <li>Paper reproductions</li>
        <li>Reinforcement learning</li>
      </ul>
    </article>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

